A||||14||Posthumane||Engine swap - small displacement||||1||
Z||000000||Posthumane||10-29-2001||09:56 PM||||Right now I have an 84 se (4cyl) and I would like to do an engine swap to something with a little more top end. I would like to retain fairly decent gas mileage due to the small tank, so I think a small displacement high revving engine would be best. I was thinking I'd like to put a quad 4 into it, but from what I hear it's a hell of a swap. For that much work I could just as well go with something from another manufacturer. I was toying with the idea of a rotary, or mabe a chrysler torbo engine. Any suggestions? I don't want anything over 3L, but more than 4 cyls is ok (3L V12 from an F1 car would be great if i could find one cheap  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ). The biggest problem I have with the quad 4 is I can't find one anywhere.||||reg||1
Z||000001||85ZainoGT||10-29-2001||10:23 PM||||go for the ls1, not to much weight difference, 28mpg+ in the vettes... a lil more power then the 4 you got right now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1985 White/Silver GT <BR>2.8L 4 Speed LOADED :)<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sigpic2529_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||AutoXdbdragSE||10-29-2001||10:31 PM||||I always thought either a saturn twin cam would be cool, or the 2.0L turbo.  those engines can be mean.. also the engine from an turbo eclipse would probably do some good in a fiero.. do lots of good.  But yeah the complexity of the swap if you went all out with new gauges would be the same as a quad four i'd think. talk to aus.. i think they have mazda cosmos over there in that austrailia place, maybe he could smuggle you a 3 rotor rotary.. hehehe.. that would be fun with three turbos.. heheheheheee  <BR>----&gt;insert big grin here&lt;----<p>[This message has been edited by AutoXdbdragSE (edited 10-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroRacer||10-29-2001||11:09 PM||||2.2L TIII Motor from a Daytona R/T.<BR>224hp<BR>217ft-lbs<BR>Forget the MPG right now.  Enough to make a 3300lb Daytona eat a 350 Camaro from that time (Excluding the 4rth gen in 93).<BR>Lotus designed heads too.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||10-29-2001||11:24 PM||||Take a jag motor and destroke it (v-12)<P>They used a TH400 (GM) tranny in a good number of the jags produced during the 70's and 80's if not all.<P>This is the same bolt patter as a 350 SBC.<P>You will likley need a shoehorn though <P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000005||artherd||10-30-2001||05:08 AM||||Take two (or three...) bigish 4-cyl motorbike engines in the 1200cc range.  Bolt together on a common crank at a 90degree angle.<P>2.4litre crazy little 12,000rpm V8!!!<P>Didn't Maseratti make a twin turbo 2.8 litre 4-cam v8 ?  Ghib Chub, or something like that?<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000006||AusFiero||10-30-2001||09:24 AM||||Ok call it sacriligious but how about a MR2 turbo engine out of a gen 2 car. 225 HP standard and easy to extract more from.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero2.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000007||malacite||10-30-2001||03:28 PM||||see! like i said. saturn engine!<BR>the new saturn twin cam makes 134 hp and is definatly reliable and has balls when called on. and there's an aftermarket for it too.<BR>i'd love to drop a saturn in my car. but the mods are just too extensive.<BR>this has been covered in tech disscussions before.<P>i would recomend the eclipse engine (2.2l turbo) i know a guy who runs 600-ish hp and somthing like 11 second times in his eclipse and his eclipse weights 2700lbs.<P>i can get time slips if you don't belive me.<P>------------------<BR>Malacite<P>Grendel-88 Fiero,tech 4<BR>'94 Saturn SW2 DOHC||||reg||1
Z||000008||Master_Sushi||10-30-2001||07:40 PM||||A quad 4 swap isn't "that" hard is it? I think if you use the auto trans form the doner car, the fiero axels will pop right in? I've heard manual swaps are a whore to do though. Even if it wasnt the High Output one, it would still be fun to have a fiero reving up to 7000RPM. Im sure they take better to modes then a duke does. LOL, I think anything does.||||reg||5
Z||000009||Standard||10-30-2001||09:44 PM||||A quad 4 swap is just as hard as swapping in any other engine that didn't come in the Fiero.  <P>They sure do look like they were made to go in there, tho  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000010||qwikgta||10-30-2001||10:11 PM||||I thought that I read somewhere that in 88 or 89 the quad 4 was going to be an optional engine.  So GM put the mounting holes in the cradle for it in 88.  I know that they didnt do it in 88 cause I have an 88 but isn't the cradle set up for one.  Just asking cause I don't know for sure.<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 66K, Header no Cat w/ Supertrapp, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, GT rear swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents, clear tails, KYB's, dropped springs.<P>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject/robsfieroproject.html   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sig_Pic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Posthumane||10-31-2001||12:14 AM||||FieroRacer - I thought about the 2.2L TIII but they are just as hard to find as the quad 4.<BR>Artherd - I actually had a very similar idea. Maybe in a year or three I will try to do something at my school, as I'm planning on majoring in mechanical engineering.<BR>Master_sushi - I'd want a high output w/ manual tranny if I was going to do a quad 4 swap, otherwise it's not worth the work in my eyes.<BR>The the eclipse engine seems like a good contender. I'll read up on this subject a little more, and I'll let you guys know when i decide on something.||||reg||1
Z||000012||AutoXdbdragSE||10-31-2001||12:31 AM||||Just thought about another option.. the nissan 2.4L similar displacement..whole lot nicer motor.. only SOHC though<P>Here's a real off one.. Volkswagen VR-6.. you wanna talk about fast.. 180hp stock.. huge perfomance following..that engine takes well to mods too.. but.. lots of custom fab to make it work.. good luck||||reg||1
Z||000013||filthyscarecrow||10-31-2001||12:52 PM||||here's one i had considered, but just didn't have the time for...<P>take a yamaha R1 rocket engine and turbocharge it. then run a chain drive to the rear wheels of the fiero, using either the stock diff or an LSD unit. i've heard wheel HP ratings on the R1 turbo of up to 300HP. you get a 13,000rpm redline, it would sound phucking awesome, and it would shave roughly 500lbs off the weight of the car. not only that, but you'd be replacing the 4 or 5 spd with a 6 speed sequential, adn for a little extra you could get an ignition cut box so you'd have shift-without-lift capability. hell, get some solenoids and rig up paddles on the steering wheel, just like a ferrari f355 F1. the car would be lighter, have a lower CG, sound way cooler, and be like nothing else in the world. sure you'd go through clutches pretty quick, but htye cost $50 and it would take you 45 min to change it... i say go for it!<BR>you could even call the car a "fiero GTR-1" cuz that's what it would be. ||||reg||1
